# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DayFlow app environment
# Copy to .env. Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are readable from app code.
#
# IMPORTANT: anything prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the JavaScript
# bundle at build time. It is visible to anyone who opens the app. Never put a
# secret here -- API keys, database URLs and JWT secrets belong in the backend
# .env only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the API lives.
#
# Leave this UNSET for local development: the app works it out on its own.
#   - web        -> http://localhost:4000
#   - Expo Go    -> the LAN IP that served the bundle, port 4000, so your phone
#                   reaches your Mac instead of talking to itself
#
# Set it explicitly when the API is not on port 4000 of the same host, e.g.
# once the backend is deployed:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL="https://dayflow-api.up.railway.app"
